From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:52:51 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] flush-sav-without-state

flush_resume, flush_eject and autosave now write the battery save when
the core gives no state, instead of returning before it, so a doze
that ends in a power off, an eject or an autosave keeps in-game
progress held in save RAM. The missing state is logged.
Generic half of suprsomething/slot.advance dbbadae (GPL-3.0),
https://github.com/suprsomething/slot.advance/commit/dbbadae
---
